# datarust Coding Guidelines for Cursor

## Framework Rules
- Use `datarust::Matrix` for 2D dense numerical operations.
- Avoid external math libraries (e.g. ndarray, nalgebra) unless explicitly opted into via feature flags.
- Prefer pipeline composition (`Pipeline::new()`) when chaining scalers and estimators.
- Reference scikit-learn behavior as the source of truth for numerical parity and hyperparameter names.

## Tools and MCP Server
- Test tools via the datarust MCP server: `https://datarust.dev/mcp`.
- Manifest card: `https://datarust.dev/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json`.
